invariant: INV-16
file: src/poly1305_vector.c
catches: poly1305_equiv_test
reason: a pass hands its sums to the next pass without the carry, so the
  next pass multiplies words far past 2^32, which the lanes' 32-bit
  operands cut, and every update of more than one pass computes a wrong
  tag. bin/poly1305_equiv_test holds the accumulator to poly1305.c's on
  calls of up to 20 groups and on random updates to 2,048 bytes.

--- old
    for (; n > pass_bytes; n -= pass_bytes) {
        pairs_sums(d, h, m, by, pairs);
        carry(h, d);
--- new
    for (; n > pass_bytes; n -= pass_bytes) {
        pairs_sums(d, h, m, by, pairs);
        h[0] = sums_narrow(d[0]);
        h[1] = sums_narrow(d[1]);
        h[2] = sums_narrow(d[2]);
        h[3] = sums_narrow(d[3]);
        h[4] = sums_narrow(d[4]);
